DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("1*(x^2-4*x+2)");
$fun_1 = Formula("3-(x^5)");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("({-6, -3, 9} U (-infinity, 18)) U {-6, -3, 9} U (-infinity, 18)");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-6, -3, 9} U (-infinity, 18) U {-6, -3, 9}");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("(((-infinity, 18)) - (-infinity, 18))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-7, 2, 9} - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-7, -5, -3, 1, 7, 9} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-7, 2, 9}))) U ({-7, -5, -3, 1, 7, 9} U {-7, -5, -3, 1, 7, 9}) U ({-7, 2, 9})");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-7, -5, -3, 1, 7, 9} U {-7, 2, 9} U ({-7, -5, -3, 1, 7, 9}) U {-7, 2, 9} U (1, infinity)");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("({-7, -5, -3, 1, 7, 9}) U {-7, -5, -3, 1, 7, 9} U (1, infinity)");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`0+15+1*10`] is equal to [_____]{25}
---

[`6*19+7/9`] is equal to [_____]{Real(114.777777778)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-7, -5, -3, 1, 7, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{-7, 2, 9\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x > 0\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cap (A \cap B) \cup (A \cup A) \cup (B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup B \cup (A) \cup B \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`(A) \cup A \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x < 18\}`]
- [`B = \{-6, -3, 9\}`]

Compute:
- [`(B \cup A) \cup B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cup A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`(A) - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 10, 10, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 3, -3, -7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<10, 10, 7>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, 10, 7>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, -3, -7>") x Compute("<10, 10, 7>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, -3, -7>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -1, -6, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 5, -10, 2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-1, -6, -9>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-1, -6, -9>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, -6, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-1, -6, -9>") . Compute("<5, -10, 2>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f'(8) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>8)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>9)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
